if(A.dB(g,A.a(["estradiol","estrogen test","e2"],k)))return"Estradiol swings across a cycle. A single number without the cycle day is easy to misread. In a textbook cycle, estrogen is often described as higher in the late follicular days and lower before bleeding. That sketch is not your lab.\n\nYour result has to be read against the day it was drawn and the range for that timing. This can explain the shape. It cannot replace the lab or the person who ordered it."
if(A.dB(g,A.a(["progesterone"],k)))return'Progesterone stays low until after ovulation, then rises for about a week. A blood test is sometimes used to ask whether ovulation happened, and the timing of the draw matters more than a single "good" number.\n\nA calendar cannot prove that rise. If you are timing bloodwork, ask the clinician which day they want. This reply will not call a result normal or abnormal from here.'
